# Feed-validation test suite cases.
#
# One case per line, pipe-separated:
#
#   name | packages | expected-libs | boot | assertions
#
#   name           short case id (used for the per-case project dir)
#   packages       space-separated feed package names to install (empty for boot-only)
#   expected-libs  space-separated shared-lib basenames to assert (optional)
#   boot           "yes" to also run the boot e2e (heavy: one image cycle), else "no"
#   assertions     named assertion set for the boot tier (default: ext+libs check)
#                  "luks-var"     -> fvl_assert_luks_var (checks dm-crypt /var active)
#                  "luks-var-tpm" -> fvl_assert_luks_var_tpm (luks-var + TPM2 token)
#                  "dm-verity"    -> fvl_assert_dm_verity (checks vroot verity active)
#
# The assertions column is optional: `_fvl_run_assertions` dispatches an
# unrecognized or empty value to the default ext+libs check, so a four-field line
# stays valid and the feature-group cases below leave it empty.
#
# Adding a test = adding a line. Names are the real feed package names
# (e.g. zeromq, not libzmq - debian renaming is not active here).
#
# name       | packages             | expected-libs   | boot | assertions
zeromq       | zeromq               | libzmq.so.5     | yes  |
# executorch ships only static libs + headers (-staticdev), so the SDK tier
# asserts libexecutorch.a lands in the ext sysroot; there is no runtime .so to
# load on a booted device, so boot is no.
executorch   | executorch-staticdev | libexecutorch.a | no   |
# One representative package per feature group. The always-on groups
# (system-base, networking, multimedia, python) use packages that land on
# every arch; the opengl-gated visual groups (graphics, qt, browsers) also run
# the boot e2e. The remaining groups are arch/distro/machine-feature gated, so
# they only assert feed presence (boot=no).
# name              | packages               | expected-libs | boot | assertions
system-base         | vim                    |               | no   |
networking          | networkmanager         |               | no   |
multimedia          | gstreamer1.0           |               | no   |
python              | python3-pip            |               | no   |
graphics            | weston                 |               | yes  |
qt                  | qtbase                 |               | yes  |
browsers            | chromium-ozone-wayland |               | yes  |
cameras             | pylon                  |               | no   |
ai                  | dx-driver              |               | no   |
cloud-aws           | greengrass-bin         |               | no   |
java                | openjdk-17-jre         |               | no   |
containers          | podman                 |               | no   |
# Boot-only cases: no packages to install, the assertion IS the test. Each runs
# one full image cycle and checks a storage/boot property inside the guest.
luks-var     |                      |                 | yes  | luks-var
luks-var-tpm |                      |                 | yes  | luks-var-tpm
dm-verity    |                      |                 | yes  | dm-verity
